WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.395
Renting a Home.

2
00:00:01.675 --> 00:00:06.134
Day 47 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.884 --> 00:00:08.908
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.188 --> 00:00:18.361
Today's goal: search for a flat, ask the right questions on a visit, negotiate rent and deposit with the landlord, and handle problems during your stay.

5
00:00:19.711 --> 00:00:20.565
Part 1.

6
00:00:20.845 --> 00:00:21.805
Key words.

7
00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:24.399
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:26.300
Word or phrase, and Meaning.

9
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.607
1BHK or 2BHK:

10
00:00:28.887 --> 00:00:50.135
1 or 2 bedrooms + hall + kitchen. furnished or semi-furnished or unfurnished: with furniture or some or none. rent or maintenance or deposit or advance: monthly cost or building charges or refundable money. broker or brokerage: agent or agent's fee. rental agreement or lease: the contract. notice

11
00:00:50.415 --> 00:01:02.084
period or lock-in period: time to inform before leaving or minimum stay. utilities: electricity, water, gas. tenant or landlord or owner: renter or owner.

12
00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:04.309
Part 2.

13
00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:05.805
Questions you'll ask.

14
00:01:07.055 --> 00:01:07.951
On the visit.

15
00:01:08.231 --> 00:01:11.025
How much is the rent, and is maintenance included?

16
00:01:11.305 --> 00:01:12.863
How much is the deposit?

17
00:01:13.143 --> 00:01:14.572
Is it fully refundable?

18
00:01:14.852 --> 00:01:16.324
Is there a lock-in period?

19
00:01:16.604 --> 00:01:18.033
What's the notice period?

20
00:01:18.313 --> 00:01:21.279
Is there 24-hour water supply or power backup?

21
00:01:21.559 --> 00:01:22.860
Is parking included?

22
00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.804
For a car or only a bike?

23
00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:26.172
Are pets allowed?

24
00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:30.015
Are there any restrictions (for example, bachelors, non-veg)?

25
00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:31.553
When can I move in?

26
00:01:32.903 --> 00:01:33.949
During your stay.

27
00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:35.722
The geyser isn't working.

28
00:01:36.002 --> 00:01:37.261
Could you get it repaired?

29
00:01:37.541 --> 00:01:38.906
Who pays for the repair?

30
00:01:39.186 --> 00:01:41.213
Can I paint the room or put up shelves?

31
00:01:41.493 --> 00:01:43.605
I'll be moving out at the end of next month.

32
00:01:43.885 --> 00:01:45.058
Here's my notice.

33
00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.151
When will I get the deposit back?

34
00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:49.397
Part 3.

35
00:01:49.677 --> 00:01:51.981
Conversation 1: visiting a flat.

36
00:01:53.231 --> 00:01:55.258
Here is how the conversation goes.

37
00:01:55.538 --> 00:01:56.391
Come in.

38
00:01:56.671 --> 00:01:58.378
This is the 2BHK.

39
00:01:58.658 --> 00:02:00.045
It's semi-furnished.

40
00:02:00.325 --> 00:02:01.925
It's nice and bright.

41
00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:03.847
How much is the rent?

42
00:02:04.127 --> 00:02:08.266
32,000 rupeesa month, plus 3,000 rupeesmaintenance.

43
00:02:08.546 --> 00:02:09.933
And the deposit?

44
00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:11.557
Six months' rent.

45
00:02:12.907 --> 00:02:14.507
The conversation continues.

46
00:02:14.787 --> 00:02:16.045
That's quite high.

47
00:02:16.325 --> 00:02:19.141
Most places nearby ask for three months.

48
00:02:19.421 --> 00:02:20.957
Would you accept three?

49
00:02:21.237 --> 00:02:22.688
Hmm, I can do four.

50
00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.525
Okay, four works.

51
00:02:24.805 --> 00:02:28.069
Is there power backup and 24-hour water?

52
00:02:28.349 --> 00:02:29.352
Yes, both.

53
00:02:29.632 --> 00:02:31.296
Is there a lock-in period?

54
00:02:32.646 --> 00:02:34.246
The conversation continues.

55
00:02:34.526 --> 00:02:37.534
Eleven-month agreement, with a two-month notice period.

56
00:02:37.814 --> 00:02:43.659
Can we add in the agreement that the deposit is returned within 15 days of moving out?

57
00:02:43.939 --> 00:02:45.134
Sure, that's fair.

58
00:02:45.414 --> 00:02:46.161
Great.

59
00:02:46.441 --> 00:02:48.446
I'd like to move in on the 1st.

60
00:02:49.796 --> 00:02:50.713
Part 4.

61
00:02:50.993 --> 00:02:54.129
Conversation 2: calling the landlord about a problem.

62
00:02:55.379 --> 00:02:57.406
Here is how the conversation goes.

63
00:02:57.686 --> 00:02:58.795
Hi Mr.

64
00:02:59.075 --> 00:03:01.934
Reddy, this is Ashish from flat 302.

65
00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:04.134
Sorry to call on a Sunday.

66
00:03:04.414 --> 00:03:05.566
No problem.

67
00:03:05.846 --> 00:03:06.891
What happened?

68
00:03:07.171 --> 00:03:09.497
There's water leaking from the bathroom ceiling.

69
00:03:09.777 --> 00:03:12.529
It started last night, and it's getting worse.

70
00:03:12.809 --> 00:03:13.982
Oh no.

71
00:03:14.262 --> 00:03:15.841
Is it from the flat above?

72
00:03:16.121 --> 00:03:17.315
I think so.

73
00:03:17.595 --> 00:03:21.350
I've put a bucket under it, and I've told the people upstairs.

74
00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.300
The conversation continues.

75
00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.689
Okay.

76
00:03:25.969 --> 00:03:27.911
I'll send a plumber tomorrow morning.

77
00:03:28.191 --> 00:03:29.577
Will someone be home?

78
00:03:29.857 --> 00:03:32.311
I'll work from home tomorrow, so yes.

79
00:03:32.591 --> 00:03:34.959
Could you also check who will pay for the repair?

80
00:03:35.239 --> 00:03:37.351
If it's from the upstairs pipe, they'll pay.

81
00:03:37.631 --> 00:03:38.633
Don't worry.

82
00:03:38.913 --> 00:03:39.852
Thank you.

83
00:03:40.132 --> 00:03:42.223
Please send me the plumber's number.

84
00:03:43.573 --> 00:03:44.533
Part 5.

85
00:03:44.813 --> 00:03:46.413
Before you sign: checklist.

86
00:03:47.663 --> 00:03:50.969
Rent, maintenance, deposit, brokerage, all in writing.

87
00:03:51.249 --> 00:03:52.871
Lock-in and notice period.

88
00:03:53.151 --> 00:03:54.729
Who pays for which repairs.

89
00:03:55.009 --> 00:03:58.423
Photos or video of the flat's condition on move-in day.

90
00:03:58.703 --> 00:04:00.815
Meter readings noted on day one.

91
00:04:02.165 --> 00:04:03.103
Part 6.

92
00:04:03.383 --> 00:04:04.301
Practice.

93
00:04:05.551 --> 00:04:09.369
Negotiate politely: the owner asks for 10 months' deposit.

94
00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:10.759
Write your reply.

95
00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:13.026
Success:

96
00:04:13.306 --> 00:04:14.394
Sample answer.

97
00:04:14.674 --> 00:04:18.919
That's much higher than other flats in this area, which ask for three to four months.

98
00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:20.757
Would you consider four months?

99
00:04:21.037 --> 00:04:23.362
I'm happy to sign an 11-month agreement.

100
00:04:24.712 --> 00:04:25.651
Part 7.

101
00:04:25.931 --> 00:04:26.976
Speak today.

102
00:04:28.226 --> 00:04:30.615
List 5 questions you'd ask before renting.

103
00:04:30.895 --> 00:04:34.309
Practise describing a home problem: what, where, since when.

104
00:04:35.659 --> 00:04:37.195
That's the end of this lesson.

105
00:04:37.475 --> 00:04:42.125
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

106
00:04:42.405 --> 00:04:48.528
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

